# Code of Conduct

## Our Standards

We want Hustle Goal Tracker to be a welcoming and respectful project.

Contributors, users, and anyone participating in the project are expected to:

- Be respectful and considerate.
- Communicate constructively.
- Focus on ideas and solutions rather than individuals.
- Accept different perspectives and experiences.
- Avoid harassment, discrimination, personal attacks, or disrespectful behavior.
- Keep discussions relevant to the project.

## Unacceptable Behavior

The following behavior is not acceptable:

- Harassment or intimidation.
- Personal attacks or insults.
- Discriminatory or hateful comments.
- Publishing private or sensitive information about others.
- Deliberately disruptive or abusive behavior.
- Any other conduct that would reasonably make the project community unsafe or unwelcoming.

## Reporting Issues

If you experience or witness inappropriate behavior related to this project, report it privately to the project maintainer rather than posting sensitive details publicly.

When possible, provide enough context to understand what happened.

## Enforcement

Project maintainers may take appropriate action when this Code of Conduct is violated, including removing inappropriate content or restricting participation in project discussions.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to project discussions, issues, documentation, and other spaces directly associated with Hustle Goal Tracker.

Thank you for helping keep Hustle Goal Tracker respectful and welcoming.
